2. Blueprint DSL layer

Goal: A declarative language to define fields, entities, and laws as blueprints.

Core primitives:

Field:[ \text{field}~F: \mathbb{R}^n \times T \rightarrow \mathbb{R}^k ]Blueprint form:

field GravityField {
  domain: R3;
  codomain: R3;
  initial: ZeroVector;
  update: uses Kernel.GravityLaw;
}

Entity (Organism):

entity Particle {
  state {
    position: R3;
    velocity: R3;
    mass: R;
  }
  interacts_with: [GravityField, WarpField];
}

Law / Kernel binding:

law GravityLaw {
  applies_to: [GravityField, Particle];
  equation: "F = -G * m1 * m2 / r^2";
  integrator: "RK4";
}

Blueprint modules:

universe { ... } — top-level container.

field { ... } — continuous structures.

entity { ... } — discrete agents.

law { ... } — dynamics.

metric { ... } — geometry/curvature definitions.

encryption { ... } — how this blueprint is sealed.

3. Field kernel layer

Goal: The mathematical engine that executes the laws.

Kernel responsibilities:

Discretization: grids, meshes, particles, or hybrid.

Time integration: explicit/implicit, fixed/variable step.

Coupling: multiple fields (gravity, warp, charge) interacting.

Constraints: invariants (energy, momentum, custom invariants).

Kernel structure:

class FieldKernel {
  register_field(F);
  register_entity(E);
  register_law(L);

  step(dt) {
    for law in laws:
      law.apply(fields, entities, dt);
    enforce_constraints();
  }
}

Special support for “warp-like” fields:

Metric-aware kernel:Fields evolve on a dynamic metric (g_{\mu\nu}(x,t)).

Blueprint example:

metric WarpMetric {
  signature: (-,+,+,+);
  definition: "g = eta + h(x,t)";
  evolves_with: WarpField;
}

4. Simulation runtime layer

Goal: Turn blueprints + kernel into a running universe.

Runtime components:

Blueprint Loader: parses DSL → internal graph.

Scheduler: manages time steps, sub-stepping, multi-rate integration.

Parallel Engine: CPU/GPU, domain decomposition, task graph.

Runtime loop:

load_blueprint("universe.emp");

kernel = build_kernel_from_blueprint(blueprint);
state  = initialize_state(blueprint);

while (not terminated) {
  kernel.step(dt);
  if (should_snapshot): save_snapshot(state);
  if (should_emit_events): push_events(state);
}

