5.2 Encryption & signing

Goals:

Integrity: blueprint cannot be altered without detection.

Authorship: only you can produce valid signed blueprints.

Access control: some fields/laws can be encrypted.

Mechanism:

Hash the canonical blueprint: [ H = \text{Hash}(\text{canonical_form(blueprint)}) ]

Sign with your private key: [ \sigma = \text{Sign}_{\text{CMB_private}}(H) ]

Embed in blueprint:

encryption {
  hash: "<H>";
  signature: "<σ>";
  scheme: "Ed25519";
}

Optional encrypted sections:

encrypted_section SecretWarpCore {
  cipher: "XChaCha20-Poly1305";
  key_derivation: "Argon2id";
  payload: "<ciphertext>";
}

Engine behavior:

On load:

Verify hash + signature against your public key.

Refuse to run if invalid (or mark as “untrusted universe”).

For encrypted sections:

Require key/passphrase or external KMS to decrypt.

6. Persistence & snapshot layer

Goal: Treat universes as versioned, cryptographically sealed artifacts.

Snapshot format:

{
  "blueprint_id": "universe-alpha-01",
  "state_hash": "<hash>",
  "time": 1234.5,
  "fields": { ... },
  "entities": { ... },
  "signature": "<σ_state>",
  "author_id": "cmb-<hash>"
}

Versioning:

Blueprint versions: 0.1.0, 0.2.0, etc.

State lineage: DAG of snapshots with parent references.

Each snapshot can be signed by you to assert “this is a canonical run”.

